{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Day With Vanessa", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Good Day", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.<br/><br/>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/><br/>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The man <span class=\"strong\">who/that</span> called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/>Which man? The man who called.<br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows <span class=\"italic\">man</span> - the noun it describes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The book <span class=\"strong\">which/that</span> I lent you was my father's.</span><br/>Which book? The book I lent you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Native speakers of English often omit the pronoun in object clauses. <br/>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The book I lent you was my father's.<br/>The exhibition we saw was enlightening.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The exhibition which we saw was enlightening, right Sal?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The park that we went to was so grassy.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Hypothetical Situations and Wishes", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the present or future.<br/>You use a similar structure to talk about wishes.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example: <br/>If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/>Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use: <span class=\"italic\">If + the Simple Past verb ... + would/could</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I married Peter,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be happy.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I exercised more,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I could be in better shape.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I were you,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be jumping up and down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can also reverse the clauses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I would be out more if I were you.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Notice that there is no comma when the result clause comes first. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>Remember to use a comma (,) after the If clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>You use a similar structure to talk about wishes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"strong\">wish</span>+ Simple Past tense ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I wish I had my camera.<br/>I wish we could do that every day. <br/>I wish I could dance as well as the go-go dancers. </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "enlightening", "type": "name"}, {"content": "giving someone knowledge", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The exhibition which we saw was enlightening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "zodiac", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a repeating cycle of 12 years, with each year being represented by an animal and its attributes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you do some reading about your zodiac sign?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "attribute", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feature", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must be curious to find out what the horse's attributes are. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dramatic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "impressive; spectacular", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Their outfits were so dramatic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vibrant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "lively; colorful; bright", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The colors were very vibrant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crisp", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cool; fresh; invigorating (when talking about the weather)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The air was so crisp.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "grassy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "covered with grass", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The park was so grassy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "go-go dancer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a dancer who entertains crowds at nightclubs", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wish could dance as well as the go-go dancers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Take turns with a partner acting out the following feelings and situations: angry, hungry, sad, excited, frustrated, scared.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can talk but don't say the adjective. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Watch your partner act and try to guess how he or she feels.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use a statement to express how you think your partner is feeling.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Act out some other feelings that you think of.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about hypothetical situations. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express complex statements. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I show I understand someone's feel